id=a52sxq_aod_brightness
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: automatic AOD brightness with wallpaper AOD
author=kusti420
description=SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_LCD_CONFIG_AOD_FULLSCREEN=1 (wallpaper AOD, sff.sh) also switches AODService to the fullscreen "platform brightness" mode: lux -> nits through config_autoBrightnessLevels_doze / config_autoBrightnessDisplayValuesNits_doze -> DisplayManager.convertToBrightness(). Those arrays exist only in the S26 Ultra's own product overlay (empty in framework-res, absent for the A52s), so the spline is null, every lux gives 0 nits -> platform brightness 0 -> HLPM 2 nit in any light. That mode also registers the sensor hub in lux-hysteresis mode, which the A52s One UI 6 AOD app never used. Keep wallpaper AOD but go back to the stock A52s brightness path: the sensor hub reports an AOD brightness index 0-3 (status 101-104) and SystemUI maps it through config_aodBrightnessValues 0/12/32/55 onto the panel's HLPM 2/10/30/60 nit levels, capped by the lock screen brightness.
